<law>
	<structure>
		<unit label="title" identifier="45.2" level="1">Mines, Minerals, and Energy</unit>
		<unit label="subtitle" identifier="III" level="2">Mineral Mines</unit>
		<unit label="part" identifier="A" level="3">Mineral Mines Generally</unit>
		<unit label="chapter" identifier="11" level="4">Mineral Mine Safety Act</unit>
		<unit label="article" identifier="5" level="5">Mine Rescue Teams</unit>
	</structure>
	<section_number>45.2-1136</section_number>
	<catch_line> Duty to train team</catch_line>
	<text>
		It is the duty and responsibility of the Department to see that every mine rescue team is properly trained by a qualified instructor of the Department or another person who has a certificate of training from the Department or MSHA.
	</text>
	<history>1997, c. 390, § 45.1-161.292:41; 2021, Sp. Sess. I, c. 387.</history>
